<article class="env-definition" id="0091">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0091">Definition <span data-tag="0091">6.25.1</span>.</a> A <em>ringed space</em> is a pair $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ consisting of a topological space $X$ and a sheaf of rings $\mathcal{O}_ X$ on $X$. A <em>morphism of ringed spaces</em> $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) \to (Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y)$ is a pair consisting of a continuous map $f : X \to Y$ and an $f$-map of sheaves of rings $f^\sharp : \mathcal{O}_ Y \to \mathcal{O}_ X$. </p>
</article>